{"description": {"type": "/type/text", "value": "Although Rudyard Kipling is chiefly remembered as the author of such classicsas _Kim_ and _The Jungle Book_, he was also a prodigious and widely read writer of verse, and is considered by many to be the poet of the British Empire. His poetry, like his fiction, gives eloquent expression to the lives of unsung men and women, children, and animals. Witty, profound, acerbic, and occasionally savage, Kipling's poetry can be both tender and deeply moving. This complete, definitive collection of his verse will delight and enthrall readers of all ages."}, "title": "Poems", "covers": [7119564], "subject_places": ["India", "Michigan"], "subjects": ["Biography", "English Authors", "English poetry", "Baltimore and Ohio Railroad Company", "Children's poetry, English", "Poetry", "British", "Railroad stations", "Works by individual poets: 19th century", "English, Irish, Scottish, Welsh", "Collected works", "Nobelpristagare", "Litteratur", "Poetry (poetic works by one author)", "Kipling, rudyard, 1865-1936", "Collected works (single author, multi-form)", "Fiction", "Social life and customs", "Po\u00e9sie anglaise", "English Ballads", "English Short stories", "Authors", "\u00c9crivains", "Biographies", "Children's poetry", "Short stories", "Adventure stories", "Mowgli (Fictitious character)", "Animals", "Jungles", "Criticism and interpretation", "English literature"], "subject_people": ["Rudyard Kipling (1865-1936)"], "key": "/works/OL15217334W", "authors": [{"type": {"key": "/type/author_role"}, "author": {"key": "/authors/OL24461A"}}, {"type": {"key": "/type/author_role"}, "author": {"key": "/authors/OL2641012A"}}], "subject_times": ["20th century", "19th century"], "type": {"key": "/type/work"}, "genres": ["/tags/OL164T"], "latest_revision": 24, "revision": 24, "created": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2010-07-16T14:00:06.338233"}, "last_modified": {"type": "/type/datetime", "value": "2026-08-29T14:44:58.281745"}}